# Milestone: v0.10.13-hygiene (v0.10.11-A)
# Covers: String.asString() idempotent overlay.
#
# Legacy share/urbi/string.u defines String.asString as the identity
# function.  The v0.6.1 stdlib reimplementation skipped it on the
# rationale that String->String is a no-op.  v0.10.11 W4 surfaced
# the gap when Lobby.echo called msg.asString() on String arguments.
#
# Tests: idempotency on literal; idempotency after concat; generic
# dispatch consistency on Integer and Float (both already have
# asString — this guards that String dispatches correctly too).

# Basic idempotency on a literal string.
"hello".asString()
[00000000] "hello"

# Idempotency on concatenated result.
("abc" + "def").asString()
[00000001] "abcdef"

# Generic dispatch consistency: Integer.asString().
(1).asString()
[00000002] "1"

# Generic dispatch consistency: Float.asString().
(1.5).asString()
[00000003] "1.5"
